sem_init accepts a semaphore shared between processes (pshared). A
semaphore is one futex word, and Radix names a word of memory several
processes map by that memory, not by each process's address, so a post
in one process wakes a waiter in another with no change to the rest of
the code (radix-address-space(2)). mlibc refused them with ENOSYS on
every system. Dukovo only: upstream would need to know which systems
share futex words.

